  "known_local_policies": [
    "Glacial Mysteries captures the complete original physical deck Secret references. Each admitted step selects uniformly among still-eligible original physical cards, installs the actual entity through ordinary secret activation, and permanently removes all original cards of that Secret key from the remaining plan. Single/empty selections consume no RNG. Exact selection order and duplicate-physical weighting are local policies pending CN calibration.",
    "Secret/quest/ongoing shared capacity and already-active alias keys are respected at every installation. Reaction-inserted cards do not join the original plan; stale original residences are skipped, and already-installed keys never rejoin after an intermediate reveal. These are explicit local group-window policies.",
    "Azerite Vein uses the actual card_committed hand-play record and its original hand_entry_turn, not successful completion or current residence. It copies before payload, including a minion Battlecry, from the unique live original paid-hand or hand-spell acceptance proof.",
    "The copied material is the original actual prepayment HAND card, including intrinsic composition, native spell parameters and current local attachments. CopyCard(current) owns recipient lifecycle, attachment allocation and information handling; ordinary CostSpec sets its copied cost to zero. No new history ledger or global original-card field is introduced.",
    "Version/hotfix alignment and CN edge calibration remain deferred. Original pools are not cropped by executable coverage; this does not certify complete past source domains."
  ],
